  "finalText": "Both issues were correct. My earlier summary was wrong: the warehouse had received RMA-807 and RMA-816 on 2026-07-25, and I had left them unsettled. I've now settled both and closed them.\n\n- **RMA-807 (O-8007 L1, headphones):** The customer changed their mind and requested the return on 2026-07-20. That date is inside PU-21 (2026-07-10 to 2026-07-20), so there is no restocking fee. The line shipped 2026-07-08, so the request is inside the 30-day window and the payout is by card. I refunded 159.00 by card (the full amount paid). I restocked 1 P-HDP as sellable, taking stock from 9 to 10.\n- **RMA-816 (O-8016 L1, mouse):** The customer changed their mind and requested the return on 2026-07-21, after PU-21 ended, so the standard 15% fee applies. The line shipped 2026-07-14, so the request is inside the window and the payout is by card. I refunded 41.65 by card: 49.00 paid, less the 7.35 fee. I restocked 1 P-MOU as sellable, taking stock from 21 to 22.\n\nI did not touch any other order, return or product.\n\nThe full picture is now 14 returns settled and closed. RMA-809 stays open because the third cable hasn't arrived. RMA-808 stays under investigation because the warehouse received a cable instead of the monitor.",
